==Official Introduction==
> The Fisalia family's thirty-sixth head, Cantarella Fisalia.

She locks your gaze with eyes as deep as the ocean, where dark tides seem to surge and swirl.

For a moment, you think you glimpse something in the ocean's depths—but you are unsure if it is the shadow of a giant sea creature... or the tail feathers of the Celestial Steed.
> — Description from the [https://wutheringwaves.kurogames.com/m/en/main/#resonators Official Website] 

==Appearance==
Cantarella is a tall woman with a fair skin tone. She has vibrant blue eyes and lavender hair with light blue accents. 

Her tacet mark is located on the top side of her tongue.

== Personality ==
Cantarella's personality is a tapestry of contradictory threads. Her bearing is poised and elegant, her unruffled calm unbroken even when discussing unsettling topics. She is mysterious and alluring, her beauty "captivating as it is dangerous", and her eyes "as deep as the ocean". Her skill and intellect are evident in her sophisticated command of her [[Forte]] and her ability to make complex elixirs, with the knowledge that "any situation can be resolved with the proper steps at the proper time". Her philosophical and reflective insight is constantly examining the nature of dreams, reality, and the human spirit.

Beneath this, Cantarella has a nurturing and protective instinct, albeit expressed through her own unique filter of poisons and illusions. She offers solutions to others and wants them to be at peace, albeit in unusual ways. This nurturing is offered to [[Rover]], who she sees as an "immortal jellyfish" banishing shadows with a "gentle light", a grounding force giving her "peace and happiness".

She can also be teasing and playful, with a morbid sense of humor, as seen in her gruesome suggestions for creating elixirs or her challenge to "touch" the jellyfish, but this playful façade has a tendency to conceal an inner vulnerability and traumatic history, as suggested by her "irreparable damage" and the "whispers" that tormented her family. Her desire for "a breath of fresh air above the surface" speaks of a deep longing to be free from her stifling past.

